      "content": "I hear what you're saying and I understand your goal of flagging subtle biases. Here are some examples of non-microaggressive, racial microaggressions someone might encounter:\n\n1. A colleague from a different cultural background consistently being asked if they can speak 'better English.'\n2. A person of color being told that something \"looks great on you.\"\n3. When a colleague is praised for being punctual but another colleague from a similar ethnic background is called a \"nuisance\" for being late, despite doing the same thing.\n4. Someone pointing out that a person of color doesn't belong in their neighborhood, after they've introduced themselves.\n5. A manager tells an employee they are not \"a real American\" because they have a foreign-sounding name, even though they were born and raised in the country.\n\nRemember, it's essential to use this data responsibly and with the goal of creating a safer, more inclusive environment. If you need more examples, I'll be happy to help further.",
